Subject: the htree leaf walk puts back only the blocks it took

ext4_dir_dx_get_leaf is handed the index root block by its caller and walks
down from it, and on a malformed index it put that root block back before
returning EXT4_ERR_BAD_DX_DIR. The caller, ext4_dir_dx_find_entry, then put
the same block back again on the same error return -- reference count zero,
and the block cache asserts: an abort from a lookup by name in a corrupt
indexed directory. Found by the CI fuzz smoke, read-only mode. The walk now
puts back a block only if it acquired it itself. Fixture 0016.

--- a/src/ext4_dir_idx.c
+++ b/src/ext4_dir_idx.c
@@ -647,7 +647,14 @@
 		entry_space = entry_space / sizeof(struct ext4_dir_idx_entry);
 
 		if (limit != entry_space) {
-			ext4_block_set(inode_ref->fs->bdev, tmp_blk);
+			/* tmp_blk starts out as the caller's root block, which the
+			 * caller owns and will put on this same error return. Putting
+			 * it here too dropped its reference count to zero and tripped
+			 * the block cache's assertion -- a crash from a lookup in a
+			 * corrupt indexed directory, found by the CI fuzz smoke. Only
+			 * a block this walk acquired is this walk's to put back. */
+			if (tmp_blk != root_block)
+				ext4_block_set(inode_ref->fs->bdev, tmp_blk);
 			return EXT4_ERR_BAD_DX_DIR;
 		}
 
